//! Painting model (the same one the sibling svg leaf writes, so an svg renderer is a usable oracle): visible layers in
//! order, each node painted source-over; a `Path` fills with the non-zero rule (every subpath implicitly closed) and then
//! strokes (butt caps, miter joins, SVG's default miter limit 4); a node without a style fills black and does not stroke,
//! exactly SVG's defaults; `opacity` multiplies both paints. A `Text` node is its value laid out on one baseline starting at
